    {
      "type": "prose",
      "caption": "Summary",
      "html": "<p>This optional unit adds 50 words that occur 16–17 times in the New Testament and are not in Machen&#x27;s lessons: 20 nouns, 19 verbs and 11 other words. Nothing in the course waits for them; they are here so that you can read the New Testament with the lexicon open less often. Learn them on the Words track: recognize, recall, type, type with accents.</p>"
    },
    {
      "type": "prose",
      "caption": "Built from words you know",
      "html": "<p>These verbs are a preposition plus a verb from the lessons; the meaning usually follows from the parts: ἐμβαίνω (βαίνω); ἐξίστημι (ἵστημι); καταλύω (λύω); κατέχω (ἔχω); ὑπομένω (μενῶ); ἀνακρίνω (κρίνω); κατακρίνω (κρίνω).</p>"
    },
    {
      "type": "prose",
      "caption": "Common confusion",
      "html": "<p>Look-alikes that differ by one letter: ἐξίστημι (I astonish) and ἐφίστημι (I stand by); μήτι (if not) and μήτε (nor); νίπτω (I wash) and πίπτω (I fall); κακῶς (badly) and κακός (bad); κλείω (I shut) and κλαίω (I weep). Feminine although they end in -ος, like ὁδός: Ἔφεσος.</p>"
    },
    {
      "type": "prose",
      "caption": "Source",
      "html": "<p>Words chosen by their New Testament frequency (MorphGNT); glosses after Jeffrey Dodson&#x27;s Greek-English lexicon (public domain).</p>"
    },
